+++ b/docs/time-off.md
@@ -0,0 +1,135 @@
+# Groomer time off and breaks
+
+Use time-off blocks for lunch, personal appointments, or a day away. They remove
+unavailable times from the booking page and reject direct bookings that overlap.
+They do not create appointments, appear on the day sheet, or generate reminders.
+
+## Open the staff screen
+
+From the Fernhill checkout, run:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m fernhill --db fernhill.db staff
+```
+
+Open **http://127.0.0.1:8001/** on that computer. The database must already contain
+your salon and groomers. Use the same database path as the booking server. The
+public booking server continues to run with `python3 -m fernhill serve` on port
+8000; the optional staff command is a separate process. To change its port:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m fernhill --db fernhill.db staff --port 8002
+```
+
+The screen includes a day view of appointments and time off, a saved-block list,
+and a form for adding blocks. Choose the groomer first. Choose a date and local
+start/end times, then select **Does not repeat** or **Every week**. An optional
+label such as “Lunch” is visible only in the staff tool. Click **Save time off**.
+The date in the form is the first occurrence, even if it differs from View day.
+
+A weekly block repeats on that weekday, from the chosen date onward, until
+removed. For a full day away, cover the salon's opening hours. Blocks can also be
+saved on closed days or outside opening hours; they do not open the salon.
+
+To remove a block, use its **Remove** button and confirm. For weekly blocks this
+removes the entire series, including its historical occurrences. Cancelling the
+dialog changes nothing. Editing means removing a block and adding its replacement;
+there is currently no single-occurrence exception or series end date.
+
+## Booking rules
+
+- A service must fit entirely outside the groomer's blocks. For example, a
+  45-minute bath at 12:00 is unavailable during a 12:30–13:00 lunch.
+- Appointments may end exactly when a block starts or start exactly when it ends.
+- Blocks affect only their assigned groomer.
+- Adding a block that overlaps an existing **booked** appointment is rejected.
+  The error names the first conflicting date/time. Move or cancel that appointment
+  through the salon's existing workflow before trying again. For weekly blocks,
+  every booked occurrence from the first date onward is checked, with no cutoff.
+  Cancelled and completed appointments do not prevent a new block.
+- Multiple overlapping blocks are allowed. Removing one leaves the other blocks
+  in place. Removing time off never removes or changes an appointment.
+- All dates and times use the salon's existing local-time convention. Blocks are
+  minute-precision, within a single calendar day; overnight blocks are rejected.
+  For overnight time off, enter a block on each affected day covering its hours.
+- The booking server rechecks availability inside the same database write
+  transaction as the booking. If staff adds a block while a client is choosing a
+  time, the client's booking is rejected if the block wins the write lock. If the
+  booking wins, adding the conflicting block is rejected instead.
+
+The last-slot closing-time behavior tracked separately in issue #2 is unchanged.
+
+## Local access and storage
+
+Fernhill does not yet have staff accounts. The staff command binds to **127.0.0.1**
+and must remain local. It is not a public admin site. Do not expose its port or
+mount `staff.make_app` in the public booking server. Staff mutation routes are not
+present in the public app.
+
+The local app restricts Host to loopback names, requires a per-process page token
+for writes, serves no CORS permissions, and refuses framing. These protect the
+local tool from other websites; they are not a replacement for staff authentication
+or OS access controls. Anyone with access to this computer can use it. A browser
+page left open across a staff-server restart must be refreshed before saving.
+
+Opening an existing database automatically creates the additive `time_off` table
+and its index with `CREATE ... IF NOT EXISTS`. Existing tables and appointments
+are preserved. Stop and restart an already-running booking process after installing
+this code so that it uses the new scheduling rules. The database itself needs no
+manual migration command. For rollback, remove blocks through the staff screen
+first; older code does not enforce them.
+
+## API and Python use
+
+These routes belong only to the local staff app:
+
+| Method and route | Result |
+|---|---|
+| `GET /api/time-off?groomer=1` | `{"blocks": [...]}`: all saved blocks, including past one-off dates |
+| `GET /api/schedule?groomer=1&date=2026-10-13` | Opening hours, booked appointments, and blocks applying that day |
+| `POST /api/time-off` | `201 {"id": 1}` or an error; JSON fields below |
+| `DELETE /api/time-off/1` | `200 {"removed": true}`, or `404` if already removed |
+
+POST takes `groomer_id` (integer), `starts_on` (`YYYY-MM-DD`), `start_time` and
+`end_time` (`HH:MM`), `repeat` (`once` or `weekly`, defaults to `once`), and `note`
+(optional, one line, at most 120 characters). JSON request bodies are limited to
+4 KB. POST and DELETE require `X-Fernhill-Token` from the current staff page.
+The UI handles this automatically.
+
+Malformed input returns `400`, existing-booking conflicts return `409`, missing or
+invalid page tokens return `403`, and database lock timeouts return `503` with a
+retry message. Reads and writes return JSON errors. The public appointment route
+continues to return `409` for bookings that overlap time off.
+
+For scripts already running locally with database access:
+
+```python
+from fernhill import db, time_off
+
+conn = db.connect("fernhill.db")
+block_id = time_off.add_block(
+    conn, groomer_id=1, starts_on="2026-10-13", start_time="12:30",
+    end_time="13:00", repeat="weekly", note="Lunch",
+)
+blocks = time_off.list_blocks(conn, 1)
+# When this block is no longer needed:
+time_off.remove_block(conn, block_id)
+conn.close()
+```
+
+Time-off writes and `scheduling.book()` own their transactions; commit or roll back
+unrelated writes before calling them. Both acquire SQLite's write lock before
+checking conflicts. No billing behavior is changed.
+
+## Verification
+
+```sh
+python3 -m unittest -v
+python3 -m compileall -q fernhill tests
+```
+
+The tests cover one-off and weekly recurrence, year/leap-day boundaries, duration
+overlaps, groomer isolation, exact boundaries, direct booking, unchanged reminders,
+conflicting future appointments, block removal, validation, legacy-database
+upgrades, persistence, simultaneous connections, the public/staff route separation,
+request protections, and the loopback CLI binding. No external service is required.
